1. Definitions

"Software" means CleanMol Discovery, including source code, documentation,
configuration files, examples, user interfaces, scripts, workflows, and
project-authored data templates distributed in this repository.

"Author" means Jonathan Graziola.

"Research Use" means noncommercial scientific research, nonprofit research,
education, teaching, personal evaluation, independent individual use, and
publication-oriented laboratory or computational investigation that is not
performed for commercial advantage or on behalf of a for-profit entity.

"Output" means any dataset, candidate molecule list, ranked candidate,
screening profile, model prompt, model output, report, review packet,
workflow artifact, analysis, or other result generated, selected, filtered,
ranked, or materially assisted by the Software.

"Discovery" means any chemical candidate, molecule, formulation idea,
antimicrobial or disinfectant lead, experimental result, patent filing,
publication, product concept, commercial product, service, regulatory filing,
or intellectual-property claim that is materially enabled by use of the
Software or an Output.

"Commercial Use" means any use that is intended for commercial advantage,
monetary compensation, product development, paid services, resale, sublicensing,
private-label distribution, hosted software-as-a-service, enterprise deployment,
for-profit internal research and development, patent monetization, investment
diligence, manufacturing, sale, licensing, or commercialization of a Discovery.

